    "introduction": "Pearson provides educational content, assessments and learning services to students, institutions and employers. Its activities include qualifications and testing, higher-education course materials, English-language learning and workforce skills. Revenue comes from products, digital subscriptions, assessment fees and service arrangements with organisations or learners. Customers use its tools to learn material, demonstrate competence and progress into further study or employment. The business depends on trusted content and reliable assessment, with technology changing how both are delivered. Demand varies across education systems and employment markets, while adoption by institutions, learner engagement and the move from printed materials to digital services influence commercial performance.",
